    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but rewriting brains sounds so exhausting. it's like fighting a war that's already been lost. if the end result is always the same—the same breakdown, the same emptiness, the same tragic exit—then isn't all this \"fighting\" just prolonging the inevitable? if the outcome is biologically determined, isn't there a certain kind of peace in just accepting it instead of struggling against the current for decades?",
